{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git log -9 --oneline && rg -n -m 3 'T-dense-donut|T-pointer-scatter' reviews/2026-11-18 -g '*.md' --glob '\"'!**/wp/scene-lookup-fix-3.report.md'\"' --glob '\"'!**/wp/acceptance-browser.fix.report.md'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"dc5f28b Status: recorded results at d8b4150; sixth core pass, test alignment, two Codex runs under way\n21130ba Briefs: donut thin slice and scatter tie; matrix re-merge\n3d547c4 Decision 0004 revision 2: the tooltip is anchored to the datum and takes no pointer events while hovered; readout mode decided by layout\nd8b4150 Acceptance wrapper: the browser configuration gets a longer time limit\ne9b4d7b Browser acceptance suite strengthened after review: 532 tests with negative controls (Claude Opus 5.5 high)\n0e5aa29 Chart core, fifth fix pass (Claude Opus 5.5 high)\ned230af Stores, reader, lookup, diagnostics: review findings fixed (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh)\n76c06bd Brief for the stores, reader, lookup and diagnostics review fixes\n93666f4 Spec: donut limit counts slices with an arc; mixed-sign stacks read both totals; shares to one fraction digit. Contract: three message keys\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/scene-lookup-fix-3.prompt.md:7:1. **T-dense-donut** (`type-matrix.browser.test.ts`, \"T-dense-donut: no simplified drawing: eight slices, the smallest under 0.2 %, are each drawn at their angle in their colour\"). The 0.1 % slice gets an empty path (`d=\"\"`): it is not drawn at all. Spec 3.6, donut row: no simplified drawing; spec A5: adjacent filled marks are separated by at least 1 px of background. The suspected cause is in the arc builder (`src/scene/index.ts` or the arcs module): the separator gap is subtracted from each slice and swallows a slice thinner than the gap. Every slice with a positive value must be drawn and identifiable (a minimum visible extent along the ring: decide and state it, for example one device pixel of arc plus the separator on each side taken from its neighbours in proportion), slices must keep their order and total sweep, and the 1 px separators must survive. Reproduce in Node from the test's fixture (read the test for the data and the plot size); then a property test (fast-check, at least 1,000 runs): for any 1 to 8 positive values spanning six orders of magnitude and any ring radius the layout can produce, every slice has a non-empty path with positive area, slices do not overlap, their order is the input order, and adjacent slices are at least 1 CSS px apart along the mid-radius.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/scene-lookup-fix-3.prompt.md:8:2. **T-pointer-scatter** (same file, \"T-pointer-scatter: two points equally near the pointer: the later row wins, whichever series it is (source order reversed, the other wins)\"). With the source rows in one order the later row wins; with the rows reversed, the same point still wins, so the winner is not decided by source row. Your lookup tests pin the later-row tie-break at the lookup's own level (commit ed230af), so either the row numbers the lookup sees are not the caller's source row indexes in this path (check how `PointSeries.row` is filled in `src/data` for long-form rows with a series field, and what `scatterGrid` compares: you may read `src/data`, and if the defect is there, say exactly where: you own that module too in general but it is outside this package's scope, so describe the fix and I will include it), or the tie is not exact in the browser because of scale rounding (two points \"equally near\" in data space project to positions that differ by a fraction of a pixel). Read the test's fixture and expected positions, reproduce in Node with the same plot rectangle, and report which it is. If it is rounding, the rule a reader needs is: distances that differ by less than half a device pixel are a tie, and ties go to the later source row; implement that in the lookup and state it for the contract comment on `Lookup.pick` in `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` (do not edit the contract; give me the sentence).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tests-codex.review.md:174:- **Matrix judgement on the sampled cells I agree with:** F1 area/bar/compact, F2 line/bar/donut/scatter (apart from finding 4), F8 donut, F11 line/area/scatter, T-pointer-scatter, T-tooltip-scatter, T-zoom-bar, T-zoom-donut, T-limit-donut, T-reference-donut, C5, F7/*, L5/* and L3/* rated weak, A6 and I4 \"cannot be verified here\" (other engines and real phones). The cited titles exist, since the checker joined them against the results.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
